{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The new.</b> I have explained it (Isaiah 65:17):" "<b>Standing before.</b> That they will not wear out like the former ones. And the sense of 'before' is because HaShem is the foundation of all standing:" "<b>So shall your seed and your name stand.</b> That it shall not be obliterated, or 'your name' (that it shall not be obliterated) like your seed, and the meaning is doubled and the sense is like 'For now it will be said to Jacob and Israel' (Numbers 23:23):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {2 "The bracketed editorial note [צ\"ל וכמוהו] ('read: and like it') is a corrected reading supplied by the editor; translated here as 'like' integrated into the comparison."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:18.810608649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}